{
  "uid": "faas-function",
  "title": "FaaS — function detail",
  "tags": ["faas"],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "editable": false,
  "refresh": "10s",
  "time": { "from": "now-30m", "to": "now" },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "function",
        "label": "Function",
        "type": "query",
        "query": "label_values(faas_processed_total, function_id)",
        "refresh": 2,
        "includeAll": false,
        "multi": false
      },
      {
        "name": "version",
        "label": "Version",
        "type": "query",
        "query": "label_values(faas_processed_total{function_id=\"$function\"}, function_version)",
        "refresh": 2,
        "includeAll": true,
        "multi": true
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "gridPos": { "h": 3, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 0 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Scoped to one `(function, version)` — the consumer group, and the unit that has its own offsets, lag, scaling and DLQ (§4.3). Leaving **Version** on *All* puts a shadow deploy side by side with the version it is shadowing, which §4.3 gets for free."
      }
    },

    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Outcome mix",
      "description": "SUCCESS / SKIPPED / FAILED. SKIPPED is a deliberate answer, not a failure — a function that cannot say anything useful about a file (silence, too short) returns nothing rather than inventing a number, and a rising SKIPPED share usually means the input mix changed.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 3 },
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "reqps", "custom": { "fillOpacity": 30, "stacking": { "mode": "normal" } } } },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (status) (rate(faas_processed_total{function_id=\"$function\", function_version=~\"$version\"}[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{status}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },

    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Per-file latency",
      "description": "Wall time from submit to outcome, which includes retries and the queueing behind a saturated pool — not just the time spent computing.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 3 },
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "s" } },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.5, sum by (le) (rate(faas_file_latency_bucket{function_id=\"$function\", function_version=~\"$version\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p50",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(faas_file_latency_bucket{function_id=\"$function\", function_version=~\"$version\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(faas_file_latency_bucket{function_id=\"$function\", function_version=~\"$version\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p99",
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ]
    },

    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Realtime multiple vs §8's floor",
      "description": "The onboarding contract, measured continuously rather than once at review time. Below 25 the concurrency this function needs (5000/speedup) grows faster than the pod count anyone budgeted for.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 11 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": { "thresholdsStyle": { "mode": "line" } },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "red", "value": null },
              { "color": "green", "value": 25 }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.5, sum by (le) (rate(faas_realtime_multiple_bucket{function_id=\"$function\", function_version=~\"$version\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p50",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.05, sum by (le) (rate(faas_realtime_multiple_bucket{function_id=\"$function\", function_version=~\"$version\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p05 (worst files)",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ]
    },

    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Backlog and in-flight depth",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 11 },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(clamp_min(kafka_consumergroup_lag{consumergroup=~\"$function:.*\"}, 0))",
          "legendFormat": "lag (messages)",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum(faas_in_flight{function_id=\"$function\", function_version=~\"$version\"})",
          "legendFormat": "in flight",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ]
    },

    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Failure ladder",
      "description": "Retries, then dead letters, by reason code. A retry that never becomes a dead letter is a dependency recovering as designed; a reason code that appears in both is one that is not.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 19 },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (reason) (rate(faas_retries_total{function_id=\"$function\", function_version=~\"$version\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "retry {{reason}}",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum by (reason) (rate(faas_dlq_total{function_id=\"$function\", function_version=~\"$version\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "DLQ {{reason}}",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
